speechtext:
I do not know;
I do not remember. These staff houses go back to 1940, and I do not know who paid for them then. I think probably they were built by the owners of the plant, which at that time was Sorel Industries Limited. We did not contribute any capital assistance, I think, until well into the end of 1940. But that is going back a long time and I would have to search the records. My hon. friend would not expect me to remember that.
The .fact of the matter is that this plant built for the government over $100 million worth of guns. They were paid for the work, as an over-all profit, 7-2 per cent. If you add in the costs that have been given here the profit was 10 per cent. If anyone can find any guns in the United States or in England that can be built for a profit less than the over-all cost plus 10 per cent, I would be very interested.
